[medium] internal/service/relational/suggestions/service.go:323 (concurrency/races)
acceptFilterForHash rechecks existing same-SSP filters inside the transaction, but it does not lock a stable resource or enforce a uniqueness constraint before creating a new filter. Two concurrent Accept calls for different pending suggestions with the same label_set_hash can both lock their own suggestion rows, both scan filters and find no matching SSP-bound filter, then both create identical SSP filters. That violates the accept-time dedupe guarantee and can produce duplicate dashboards for the same SSP label set.
Suggested fix: Serialize filter creation per SSP/label-set hash, for example by taking a transaction-scoped advisory lock keyed by sspID and hash before scanning/creating filters, or by persisting a canonical label-set hash on SSP-bound filters with a unique constraint and retrying/load-on-conflict.
Guidance: Fix internal/service/relational/suggestions/service.go in SuggestionService.acceptFilterForHash. Before any call to loadSameSSPFilterWithHash and before the tx.Where("ssp_id = ?", sspID).Find(&filters) scan, take a transaction-scoped lock that is stable for the SSP plus canonical label_set_hash, then perform the existing recheck/scan/create logic while holding that lock. Preferred PostgreSQL approach: add a small helper such as lockAcceptFilterHash(tx, sspID, hash) that executes SELECT pg_advisory_xact_lock($key1, $key2) or equivalent using deterministic 32-bit keys derived from sspID.String()+":"+hash with a cryptographic/hash package; do not use Go's map/hash randomization or anything process-local. Call it at the top of acceptFilterForHash so concurrent Accept calls for the same SSP/hash serialize even when they locked different suggestion rows. Keep the existing same-SSP-only filter behavior, CanonicalizeFilter/CanonicalLabelSetHash comparison, and BuildLabelFilter creation exactly as-is; do not extend or modify global filters and do not change canonical hash semantics. Make the helper safe for non-Postgres test DBs if this package uses SQLite in tests, for example by no-oping or using an existing dialect check outside production Postgres, and add an integration/unit test that runs two concurrent accepts for different pending suggestions with the same label_set_hash and asserts only one SSP-bound filter is created and both suggestions point at it.
